From: CB1 backport maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] GBM colour range, format and depth preferences with CB1 ownership

Backport smp79 Kodi PRs 30099 and 30192 once, in dependency order, from
9fcc80c946fc94f8fdcbe899a15baa0453bd6d63 and
6cc7650a603fc06992326742def234c27728e310 (both open, not merged).

Keep ordinary connector preferences separate from dedicated CB1 transports.
Reuse the native snapshot owner for Full/RGB/depth overrides and accepted
restoration, preserve CB1 software range until restoration, and reapply
preferences before the next ordinary range query. Refuse range-changing
frames without substituting their pixels into the old connector request.
Reconfigure on source-depth changes before Adaptive/shader selection.

The optional color format setting requires an offered connector property;
this does not backport the Linux 7.3 DRM property to Linux 7.2.6.

